      "message": "This `do-while` loop structure can lead to an infinite loop if `h` is an odd number. Since this function processes two rows at a time, `h` is expected to be even. \n\nConsider adding an assertion `assert(h % 2 \u003d\u003d 0);` at the beginning of the function or for the paths that use this kind of loop to ensure this invariant holds. Alternatively, a `for` loop (`for (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c h; i +\u003d 2)`) would be safer as it handles any `h` value correctly.",
